Validates z/OSMF JWK endpoint connectivity as a pre-flight check before starting Zowe.

This command reads the Zowe YAML configuration to determine the z/OSMF host, port,
authentication provider, JWT autoconfiguration mode, and certificate verification
settings. It then invokes the pre-flight-check tool to verify that the z/OSMF JWK
endpoint at /jwt/ibm/api/zOSMFBuilder/jwk is reachable.

Pre-validation checks performed before calling the JWK endpoint:
- Verifies the gateway auth provider is "zosmf" (skips if "saf")
- Verifies jwtAutoconfiguration is "jwt" (warns if "ltpa")
- Reads verifyCertificates and passes it to the pre-flight check
- Resolves truststore path from the Zowe certificate configuration

A successful result means the z/OSMF JWK endpoint is reachable and will be
available when Zowe API ML starts.
